    {
      "type": "paragraph",
      "content": "Under a flexible exchange rate system, the value of a currency is determined by the demand and supply of foreign exchange in the forex market.",
      "id": "mtjb6cj"
    },
    {
      "type": "paragraph",
      "content": "A. Demand for Foreign Exchange arises due to:",
      "id": "dyhyq6k"
    },
    {
      "type": "paragraph",
      "content": "• Imports of goods and services<br/>• Foreign travel, education and medical expenses<br/>• Interest and dividend payments abroad<br/>• Capital outflows and investment abroad",
      "id": "xct4ow2"
    },
    {
      "type": "paragraph",
      "content": "B. Supply of Foreign Exchange arises due to:",
      "id": "ww2y34q"
    },
    {
      "type": "pullQuote",
      "content": "Under a flexible exchange rate system, the value of a currency is determined by the demand and supply of foreign exchange in the forex market.",
      "id": "jhjmuaw"
    },
    {
      "type": "paragraph",
      "content": "• Exports of goods and services<br/>• Remittances from NRIs<br/>• Foreign Direct Investment (FDI)<br/>• Foreign Portfolio Investment (FPI)<br/>• External borrowings",
      "id": "xkdr1wm"
    },
    {
      "type": "paragraph",
      "content": "Equilibrium exchange rate is determined at the intersection point of demand and supply curves. If demand for dollars increases, rupee depreciates. If supply increases, rupee appreciates.",
      "id": "3p9d1ud"
    },
